In addition, the speed of sound, \(c_{s}^{2}\), which is defined as the change in pressure with respect to that of energy density at constant volume \((\frac{\partial P}{\partial\epsilon})_{V}\), vanishes at \(T_{c}\) as shown in Fig 1.8. This decrease in speed of sound is because of the production of resonances where there is no increase in kinetic energy in the system. This behavior is observed in lattice QCD calculations [25].

Various QCD based model calculations and Lattice simulation predict different points in the QCD phase diagram to be the critical point as shown in Fig. 1.9. The exact location of the critical point may be accessed through the Heavy-Ion-Collisions

